  "note": "Licence claims and what the policy of DEPENDENCIES.md makes of them. Read by backend/tests/unit/test_licence_gate.py and by frontend/src/test/licence-gate.test.ts, so that the Python gate and the npm gate cannot drift apart. 'shared' is the set the two gates' own forbidden checks agree on exactly, and both suites assert every verdict in it. 'npm_only' is spellings npm publishes and PyPI does not: the npm gate reads each word of a claim from its start and refuses them, while the Python gate reaches them only after resolving an alias, so its raw check reads them as unknown. The Python suite therefore asserts of 'npm_only' only that nothing in it is ever ALLOWED there -- which is the part that would let something through. 'restricted' is the MPL-2.0 family however it is spelt: the npm gate must call every one of them restricted, so that no 'runtime' row can carry one, and the Python gate must never call one allowed.",
